# Evidence, not claims.
#
# Every line here is a command run on the booted appliance and a string its
# output must contain. The README quotes this file's results and says nothing
# else: "no login prompt" is a fact a reader can reproduce, "hardened" is an
# assertion about attacks nobody has tried yet.
#
# ci/boot-test.sh runs these over the serial console. Because this image has
# no getty, it runs them through the QEMU monitor's console instead — see the
# script's --no-login mode.

# Nothing is listening except the tunnel. The scan that matters runs from the
# host and is in boot-test.sh; this is the view from inside.
ss -tulpn	51820

# The root filesystem is read-only, so a write fails rather than succeeding
# and being lost.
touch /test	Read-only file system

# No login prompt on any console.
ps aux	!getty

# Root has no password to guess, reuse or find in a repository: the locked
# field, not a hash.
cat /etc/shadow	root:*

# The whole of /usr/bin, printed rather than grepped: a reader can see there
# is no shell server, no interpreter and no compiler, instead of taking a
# list of six absences on trust.
ls /usr/bin	wg

# The tunnel works, which is the point of the appliance and not incidental.
wg --version	wireguard-tools
